{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00333","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00333@rel:R25-11#ea333842","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00333","release":"R25-11","content":"function RecoverKeyValueStorage [SWS_PER_00333] Upstream: RS_PER_00003 , RS_PER_00009 , RS_PER_00010 , RS_AP_00119 , RS_AP_00120 , RS_AP_00121 , RS_AP_00127 , RS_AP_00128 , RS_AP_00129 , RS_AP_00135 , RS_AP_00137 , RS_AP_00139 , RS_AP_00159 ara::core::Result &lt; void &gt; RecoverKeyValueStorage (const ara::core::InstanceSpecifier &amp;kvs) noexcept; Recovers a Key-ValueStorage. RecoverKeyValueStorage allows to recover a Key-Value Storage when the redundancy checks fail. It will fail with kResourceBusy when the Key-Value Storage is currently open, or when it is modified by a call from another thread to UpdatePersistency, CleanUpPersistency, Reset Persistency, RecoverKeyValueStorage, or ResetKeyValueStorage. This method does a best-effort recovery of all key-value pairs. After recovery, keys might show outdated or initial value, or might be lost. Header-Datei #include \"ara/per/key_value_storage.h\" class mono Scope namespace ara::per class mono Exception-Sicherheit exception safe class mono Thread-Sicherheit thread-safe class mono Parameter (in) th Parameter th Beschreibung td kvs td The shortName path of a PortPrototype typed by a PersistencyKey ValueStorageInterface. Rückgabewert th Typ th Beschreibung td ara::core::Result &lt; void &gt; td A Result of void. In case of an error, it contains any of the errors defined below, or a vendor specific error. Fehler th Fehlercode th Beschreibung td PerErrc ::kStorageNotFound td rollback_semantics Returned if the passed InstanceSpecifier does not match any PersistencyKeyValueStorageInterface configured for this Executable. td PerErrc ::kPhysicalStorageFailure td no_rollback_semantics Returned if access to the physical storage fails. td PerErrc ::kEncryptionFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if the encryption of stored data fails. td PerErrc ::kResourceBusy td rollback_semantics Returned if UpdatePersistency, CleanUpPersistency, or Reset Persistency is currently being executed, or if ResetKeyValue Storage is currently being executed for the same Key-Value Storage, or a SharedHandle of the same Key-Value Storage is currently in use. td PerErrc ::kOutOfStorageSpace td no_rollback_semantics Returned if the available physical storage space is insufficient for the recovered values. td PerErrc ::kQuotaExceeded td rollback_semantics Returned if the recovered values would exceed the configured maximumAllowedSize of the Key-Value Storage. td PerErrc ::kAuthenticationFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if calculating the MAC of stored data fails.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"baseline_sync"},"recorded_at":"2026-09-30T16:43:34+00:00","text_key":"bbba43813182"}],"lifecycle":{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00333","is_dropped":false,"first_active_release":"R25-11","last_active_release":"R25-11","dropped_in":[],"first_dropped_release":null,"absent_before":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11"],"platform_releases":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"latest_platform_release":"R25-11"},"element":{"kind":"function","name":"RecoverKeyValueStorage","module":"PER","cluster":"","page":"namespaces/ns_per_ara_per_d9a3e9.html","doc_type":"SWS","ai":false,"first":"R25-11","last":"R25-11","changed":[],"distinct":1,"universe":"AP"},"evidence":{"figures":[{"id":"FIG-b045d30e3c97fa76","doc":"AUTOSAR_AP_EXP_SWArchitecture","p":90,"rel":[],"role":"constitutive","conf":0.95,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"RecoverKeyValueStorage API in Persistency","n":16,"cap":"Figure 9.36: Interfaces for key-value-based data storage","sha":"b045d30e3c97fa76804aee0624930cbac3f6a04b3d15be2ecbb043d7043e46b6","nser":5,"src":"figure"},{"id":"FIG-a8fa6e1339537fa9","doc":"AUTOSAR_AP_EXP_SWArchitecture","p":96,"rel":[],"role":"heuristic","conf":0.85,"rt":"","m":"ge